# ==============================================================================
# Environment Configuration Overview
# ==============================================================================
# This project maintains separate configurations for Development and Production:
#
# 1. DEVELOPMENT (.env.development):
#    - Used for local testing, hot reloading, and debugging.
#    - Run locally using: npm run dev:backend & npm run dev:frontend
#    - Or using Docker dev mode: npm run dev:docker
#
# 2. PRODUCTION (.env.production.example):
#    - Template used for deployment on AWS Lightsail / VPS / Docker Compose.
#    - Reverse proxy handles SSL and routes /api requests to backend container.
#    - Run using: npm run prod:docker
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Authentication Environment Variables
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get your Client ID from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 1. Create a project in Google Cloud Console.
# 2. Go to APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen and set it up.
# 3. Go to Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID.
# 4. Choose "Web application".
# 5. Add authorized JavaScript origins:
#    - Dev:  http://localhost:3000
#    - Prod: https://yourdomain.com
# 6. Copy the Client ID below:

NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id_here.apps.googleusercontent.com
